From f7261c88c3793897f46305dfe4481daa54c78e6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Singh <nathan.singh@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:51:38 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Arena: the shop-style icon menu and the party manager's
 screens

Main-image code the arena overlay reaches through far calls:
- window/screens/arena_icon_menu.c (a part of screens.c): ArenaMenu_IconChoose,
  a prompt window across the top and a row of command icons across the bottom,
  as the shops draw them; exported in WINDOW.S.
- shop/shop/arena_shop.c (a part of shop.c): ItemPicker_ChooseMember, the
  shops' strip of walking figures with the member's items, Djinn, Psynergy or
  status beside it, and ArenaShop_Run, the stat, Djinn and Psynergy counters
  built like the shops' Buy counter; exported in SHOP.S.
They live in the main image because they use private state that overlays cannot
reach. The shop bank's neighbour moves up 0x1000 in main.ld to make room.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
